[2026-01-30T14:14:35.363Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01BhTnTJhiaiMEuUSKfmm41f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EMntzMrxZPBAuunnHFCp2f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/direction1_content.md << 'DIRECTION_EOF'\n## Vision\nConsolidate the duplicated theme-aware color mapping logic into a centralized theming utility system that provides consistent color palettes across all badge, card, and visualization components.\n\n## Business Value\n- Reduces code duplication across 10+ components that define identical light/dark color mappings\n- Single source of truth for color consistency when theme requirements change\n- Faster development of new themed components with pre-built utilities\n- Easier A/B testing of color schemes without touching multiple files\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Extract badge color configurations (TypeBadge, SourceTypeBadge, PriorityBadge, StatusBadge)\n- Consolidate card background/border color mappings\n- Create theme-aware utility hooks and classes\n- Migrate existing components to use the new system\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- Changing the visual design of any component\n- Adding new themes beyond radar/swiss\n- Modifying the ThemeContext provider itself\n\n## Key Components\n1. `shared/themeColors.ts` - Centralized color palette definitions for both themes\n2. `useThemedColors` hook - Returns appropriate colors based on current theme\n3. Updated badge components using the centralized system\n4. Updated card components using the centralized system\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Audit all files for repeated theme color patterns (lightColors/darkColors objects)\n2. Create comprehensive color palette type in `themeColors.ts`\n3. Build `useThemedColors(category)` hook that returns appropriate palette\n4. Create Tailwind-compatible class generators\n5. Migrate components one category at a time (badges first, then cards)\n6. Remove duplicate color definitions from individual components\n\n## Files to Modify\n- `src/components/report/shared/themeColors.ts` - NEW: Central color definitions\n- `src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx` - Remove inline colors, use centralized\n- `src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx` - Remove inline colors, use centralized\n- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx` - EntityTypeCard uses inline colors\n- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx` - perspectiveColors object\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx` - priorityColors inline definition\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] No component defines its own lightColors/darkColors mapping\n- [ ] All badge components use shared color utility\n- [ ] Theme color changes can be made in single file\n- [ ] Type safety for color palette access\n- [ ] No visual regression in either theme\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Component-specific color needs may not fit generic palette (mitigation: allow component-level overrides)\n- Tailwind class purging with dynamic class generation (mitigation: use safelist or static class references)\nDIRECTION_EOF\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":128803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b50487e-569d-4a38-aca7-0add610c3dda","uuid":"f05beb79-ba53-412c-8a3a-cac9253e8231"}
